# Python tooling — use uv

This monorepo manages the FastAPI app (`apps/api`) with **[uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)**. Do not use `pip`, `pip install`, or `python -m pip` in docs, CI, Docker, or agent-run commands.

## Install / sync dependencies

From `apps/api`:

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
```

Commit `apps/api/uv.lock` when dependencies change.

## Run commands

Always prefix tools with `uv run` (from `apps/api`):

```bash
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check app tests
```

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ BAD
pip install -e "./apps/api[dev]"
python -m pytest
uvicorn app.main:app --reload

# ✅ GOOD
cd apps/api && uv sync --extra dev
cd apps/api && uv run pytest
cd apps/api && uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
```

Docker and GitHub Actions must use `uv sync` and `uv run` the same way.
